#
# sources - WDK 7.1 build description for xhcimsi.sys, the NT 6 x86 MSI
# helper (design record 18; roadmap-hcd.md tasks 36.15 and 36.16), a third
# binary beside xhci98.sys and xhciuas.sys, installed only by the Vista and
# 7 x86 install path of xhci98.inf.
#
# WDK 7.1, x86, Vista target - `setenv <WDK> fre|chk x86 WLH no_oacr` - and
# nothing else: the x86 HCD and xhciuas.sys stay on MSVC 6 and the Windows
# 2000 DDK. The helper imports IoConnectInterruptEx and
# IoDisconnectInterruptEx, which only WDK 7.1's wlh\i386 ntoskrnl.lib and
# wdm.h declare (design record 18 section 8.1). Built by
# scripts\build-driver.cmd for every x86 flavour, after xhciuas.sys, and
# checked by the import gate's nt6x86 profile against
# scripts\import-gate\xhcimsi-imports.allow. Output: src\msi86\objfre\i386\
# xhcimsi.sys (release), objchk (debug), objchk_qemu (qemu).
#
# The /GS cookie stays on, the kit's default: the wdmsec.lib members that
# IoCreateDeviceSecure brings are compiled with cookie checks, so the image
# initialises the cookie through GsDriverEntry (record 18 section 8.1).
#
# ..\xhci_msi86.c is the channel's pure half, shared with xhci98.sys and the
# host suite (test\test_msi.c); XHCI_MSI86_HELPER makes its header take its
# types from ntddk.h rather than xhci_compat.h.
#

TARGETNAME=xhcimsi
TARGETTYPE=DRIVER
TARGETPATH=obj

INCLUDES=$(DDK_INC_PATH)

C_DEFINES=$(C_DEFINES) -DXHCI_MSI86_HELPER

TARGETLIBS=$(DDK_LIB_PATH)\wdmsec.lib

SOURCES=msi86_entry.c     \
        ..\xhci_msi86.c   \
        xhcimsi.rc

!IF "$(XHCI_EXTRA_DEFINES)" != ""
!ERROR XHCI_EXTRA_DEFINES is set, and xhcimsi.sys has no diagnostic builds. Clear it before building.
!ENDIF

#
# The three flavours, derived from BUILD_ALT_DIR exactly as src\sources
# derives them for xhci98.sys (design record 08), so the same flavour
# marker check and packaging refusals apply to this binary. The qemu flavour
# adds the XhciMsiInject switch (record 18 section 2.1) and nothing else.
#
!IF "$(BUILD_ALT_DIR)" == "chk_qemu"
C_DEFINES=$(C_DEFINES) -DXHCI_FLAVOUR_QEMU
!ELSEIF "$(BUILD_ALT_DIR)" == "chk"
C_DEFINES=$(C_DEFINES) -DXHCI_FLAVOUR_DEBUG
!ELSEIF "$(BUILD_ALT_DIR)" == "fre"
C_DEFINES=$(C_DEFINES) -DXHCI_FLAVOUR_RELEASE
!ELSE
!ERROR BUILD_ALT_DIR is "$(BUILD_ALT_DIR)" and this tree knows exactly three flavours - fre (release), chk (debug) and chk_qemu (qemu). Build through scripts\build-driver.cmd.
!ENDIF

!IF "$(_BUILDARCH)" != "x86"
!ERROR xhcimsi.sys is the x86 helper alone (design record 18): the amd64 HCD reaches IoConnectInterruptEx through MmGetSystemRoutineAddress and has no helper.
!ENDIF
